    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **254 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added an `initials` field to the owner API response.\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a new read-only `initials` property on the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`). The `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time, so this creates the field.\n\n**2. `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped the new field via a MapStruct expression backed by a small helper:\n\n```java\n@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")\nOwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n\ndefault String initials(Owner owner) {\n    return owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase()\n            + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\";\n}\n```\n\nFor firstName `\"john\"` / lastName `\"smith\"` this returns `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec (upper-cased first letters, dot-separated, trailing dot). `firstName`/`lastName` are required with `minLength: 1` in the schema, so the leading character always exists.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` passes, and the full suite remains green.",
